# Vestia Design Constitution

Fonte completa: `docs/VESTIA_DESIGN_CONSTITUTION.md`  
Tokens: `src/theme/colors.ts`, `src/theme/typography.ts`

## Product

Vestia is an AI Personal Stylist assistant — not fashion browsing, not e-commerce, not a closet organizer. Every UI decision must reinforce a calm, premium assistant.

## Philosophy

Less UI. More Intelligence. Prefer removing decisions, fields, and buttons when the Stylist can infer.

## Visual

- Background `#FAF8F6` · Surface `#FFFFFF` · Primary `#121212` · Secondary `#C8A97E` · Accent `#EDE5DA` · Border `#ECE7E2` · Muted `#8E8A83`
- Typography: Playfair Display (headings) + Inter (body) only — never a third family
- Spacing: 4 / 8 / 16 / 24 / 32 / 40 / 48 / 64 only
- Radius: inputs 16 · cards 24 · sheets 32 · buttons 999
- Shadows: very subtle; prefer white-on-white depth
- Color mix ≈ 90% cream/white · 8% black · 2% accent — never colorful or gamified UI

## Components

- One primary CTA per screen (solid black / white text); secondary is outline
- No gradients, filled icons, heavy borders, bounce, or confetti
- Cards: image-first, generous whitespace, minimal copy
- Icons: outline, 2px stroke
- Motion: slow fade / opacity / scale 0.98→1

## Screens & copy

- Home is an assistant (“Seu look está pronto.” / Today's Edit) — never a dashboard of metrics first
- Prefer “Nova peça”, “Stylist”, “Today's Edit” over “Adicionar roupa”, “IA”, “Sugestão”
- Voice: image consultant, never influencer slang

## Before shipping UI

1. Can we remove a button?
2. Can the Stylist decide this?
3. Can we show less?
4. Can we add more whitespace?
